The door opens and the doctor calls my name.
"Frau Flores, please!" he says cordially.
I stand up slowly and walk into the consultation room.
"Good morning, please take a seat," the doctor says.
I sit down on the small chair.
"How are you doing today?" he asks me.
I answer honestly, because I really feel terrible.
"I am not doing well at all," I say.
I point to my head and to my throat.
"My head hurts, and my throat hurts," I explain.
The doctor nods and looks at me attentively.
"And my chest hurts too," I add.
I think about my sport on Thursday evening.
Today is Wednesday, and I do not have much hope.
But I ask the doctor anyway.
"Can I play badminton tomorrow evening?" I ask quietly.
The doctor looks at me in surprise.
He folds his hands and shakes his head.
